  <h2 id="files">Files and retention</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Files upload only when you start a tool. After type and size checks, the API stores accepted content in private temporary storage; file bytes are not stored in the application database or queue messages.</li>
    <li>Retention is configurable and defaults to 60 minutes. The tool panel displays the active period reported by the API. When files expire they become inaccessible and the cleanup process performs physical deletion.</li>
    <li>A “Delete files” request immediately closes access. Deleted bytes are held through a 2-minute cleanup grace period, then removed by a periodic cleanup run; active file use can extend this. The request does not mean physical deletion has already finished.</li>
    <li>Conversion does not send document contents to an external conversion or AI service. This is separate from technical request data processed by hosting, CDN/network or measurement providers.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="session">Session and technical data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not ask for your name, phone or email to create an account. If you email us, we use the contact details you provide to reply.</li>
    <li>A signed, anonymous session cookie links API uploads and jobs to the same browser session; it expires after 24 hours. It does not contain document content.</li>
    <li>The application derives a keyed hash from the network address for request limiting and abuse prevention. Hosting, DNS/CDN and network providers may separately process IP and connection data to deliver and protect requests.</li>
    <li>Your interface language choice is stored in browser local storage.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="measurement">Site measurement</h2>
  <p>Cloudflare adds Cloudflare Web Analytics to the live domain for page-view and performance measurement. Cloudflare also handles requests as the CDN/network provider. The analytics preference control does not change Cloudflare configuration.</p>
  <p>PostHog EU loads only after you explicitly allow it. It may measure page and tool visits, API-accepted uploads, processing states observed by the browser, download clicks and fixed error categories. PostHog receives technical request data and an anonymous analytics identifier separate from file-access sessions. File names/content, passwords, file/job IDs and download URLs are excluded from analytics events. Session replay, automatic click capture and raw error/console collection are disabled. You can withdraw permission using “Analytics preferences” in the footer; this preference does not turn off advertising or Cloudflare Web Analytics. See <a href="https://posthog.com/privacy" rel="nofollow">PostHog’s Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="advertising">Advertising</h2>
  <p>A Google AdSense ad may appear on the home page. When an ad loads, Google and its partners may process data such as browser/device details, IP address and ad interactions, and may use cookies or similar technologies for ad delivery. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="nofollow">Google’s advertising technology information</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="nofollow">Google’s Privacy Policy</a> for details and controls. Uploaded document files and contents are not sent in advertising events.</p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>For privacy questions, email <a href="mailto:destek@doctorconverter.com" class="text-accent underline">destek@doctorconverter.com</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
